Seven hexagonal patches (logo in the centre, six data petals that tile the hex
lattice exactly), a binary header ring, solid inner/outer hexagons, 1 or 2 bits
per cell (2/4 Gray-coded ink levels), runs merging same-level neighbours,
homography-based hexagon detection, blind level clustering, petal-level erasure
resilience. The ring format is kept at tag rings-v1.
